 "text": "Hello! How are you today? Not quite. A century is 100 miles in single day. Most people aim for about ten hours, with stops for food and rest. That depends on your current fitness. A first ride of about twelve hours is good goal, and then you can push longer. It is. Plan rest night before and during it, and take small breaks every hour. Most people finish feeling really proud rather than horribly tired. That's a great way to build up. Doing it with friends adds motivation too. Start with shorter rides a few times week, building up distance. Add some hilly rides in the middle to mimic the terrain.",
